'''bicessis''' (bī-ses′is), ''n.'' [L., < ''bic-'', a reduced form of ''viginti'', = E. ''twenty'', + ''as'' (''ass-''), an as, a unit: see ''as''<sup>4</sup>.] In ''Rom. metrology'', twenty asses.

'''biche†''', ''n.'' [< F. ''biche'', OF. also ''bisse'' = Walloon ''bih'' = mod. Pr. ''bicho'' = It. dial. ''becia'', a hind or roe; of uncertain origin.] A kind of fur; the skin of the female deer.

'''bichir''' (bich′ėr), ''n.'' [Native name.] A remarkable living ganoid fish, ''Polypterus bichir'', of the family ''Polypteridæ'' and order ''Crossopterygii'', inhabiting the Nile and other African rivers, attaining a length of 18 inches, and esteemed as food. See ''Polypterus''.
